✅2.4 Thread Lifecycle with Runnable

After:

thread.start();

The Thread object moves through the lifecycle:

 NEW
  | start()
  ▼
 RUNNABLE
  |   ▲
  |   | Lock acquired
  | BLOCKED
  | wait(), join(), park()
  ▼
 WAITING
  | notify(), notifyAll(), interrupt()
  ▼
 RUNNABLE
  | sleep(), wait(timeout), join(timeout)
  ▼
 TIMED_WAITING
  | timeout expires / notify()
  ▼
 RUNNABLE
  | run() finishes
  ▼
 TERMINATED

 Explanation

 🔴 The lifecycle belongs to the Thread object.
 🔴 A Runnable object does not have a lifecycle.
 🔴 Multiple Thread objects can execute the same Runnable object.